schema ObsidianVaultBinding
generation obsidian-1
authority BonfyreObsidian + calling account boundary

field account
  type text
  required true
  role account-subject-as-named-by-the-caller
field name
  type text
  required true
  role per-account-vault-name
field vault_id
  type text
  required true
  role desktop-registry-id-or-local-digest
field local_path
  type text
  required true
  role real-path-inside-an-allowed-root
field transport
  type enum[cli,headless,files]
  required true
  role how-reads-writes-and-sync-reach-the-vault
field sync_mode
  type enum[bidirectional,pull-only,mirror-remote]
  required true
field conflict_strategy
  type enum[merge,conflict]
  required true
field excluded_folders
  type set[text]
  role headless-sync-and-snapshot-exclusions
field device_name
  type text
  required true
field remote_vault
  type text
  role remote-vault-id-or-name-given-to-ob
field config_dir
  type text
  required true
  role obsidian-settings-folder-never-written
field state
  type enum[bound,sync-configured,syncing]
  required true

invariant one-folder-one-account
  statement a real folder is bound at most once across all accounts, and never inside or around another bound folder
invariant same-answer-for-foreign-and-absent
  statement a verb naming a vault another account bound is refused exactly as a vault nobody bound, so names cannot be probed
invariant allowed-roots
  statement local_path is the folder's real path after symlinks and must lie inside one of the configured roots
forbidden_inference a binding -> the account owns, pays for or may share the remote Obsidian vault
forbidden_inference an account name on a binding -> that the caller authenticated as that account; the calling boundary authenticates

schema ObsidianNoteRef
generation obsidian-1
authority BonfyreObsidian

field path
  type text
  required true
  role vault-relative-slash-path
field sha256
  type text
  role bytes-read-or-written

invariant contained
  statement no empty, dot or dot-dot component, no dot-led component, never the config folder whatever its case; reads resolve inside the vault's real root, writes refuse a symlink anywhere on the path
forbidden_inference a note path -> the note exists in the app's index; the app may not have rescanned yet

schema ObsidianTaskRef
generation obsidian-1
authority BonfyreObsidian

field ref
  type text
  required true
  role path-colon-line
field status
  type enum[todo,done,other]
  required true
field mark
  type text
  required true
forbidden_inference a task ref -> a stable identity; line numbers move when the note is edited

schema ObsidianGuardDecision
generation obsidian-1
authority BonfyreObsidian

field decision
  type enum[allow,refuse]
  required true
field code
  type enum[clear,transport,desktop-sync-enabled,desktop-sync-reported,headless-other-account,headless-unscoped]
  required true
field reason
  type text
  required true
field evidence
  type text

invariant refuse-when-unclear
  statement desktop Sync and Headless Sync never run on one device for one vault; the Sync core plugin enabled, a running app reporting Sync, or another headless setup for the folder each refuse
forbidden_inference allow -> desktop Sync is off for this vault; only this device's settings and running app were read

schema ObsidianSyncRun
generation obsidian-1
authority BonfyreObsidian + Obsidian Headless

field run_id
  type u64
  required true
field receipt_id
  type text
  required true
field kind
  type enum[sync-setup,sync-config,sync-once,sync-start]
  required true
field argv
  type text
  required true
  role never-holds-a-secret
field exit_code
  type i64
  required true
field outcome
  type enum[ok,failed,timed-out,started]
  required true
field log_path
  type text
  required true
forbidden_inference outcome ok -> the remote vault and the folder agree; ob reported success for one pass

schema ObsidianReceipt
generation obsidian-1
authority BonfyreObsidian

field receipt_id
  type text
  required true
field verb
  type text
  required true
field binding
  type text
  required true
field target
  type text
  required true
field outcome
  type enum[ok,refused,failed]
  required true
field via
  type enum[cli,native,headless]
  required true
field sha_before
  type text
field sha_after
  type text

invariant no-content
  statement a receipt holds paths, digests, codes and reasons; never note content and never a credential

schema ObsidianSnapshot
generation obsidian-1
authority BonfyreObsidian

field snapshot_id
  type u64
  required true
field files
  type u64
  required true
field manifest_digest
  type text
  required true
  role sha256-over-path-sha-size-lines
field rehashed
  type u64
  required true
field reused
  type u64
  required true

invariant incremental
  statement a file whose size and mtime match the previous snapshot keeps its recorded sha256; every other file is hashed again
forbidden_inference equal size and mtime -> equal bytes; a writer that restores mtime would be missed until a full rehash
